**Create deployment** — `POST /accounts/demo/workers/scripts/demo-api/deployments`
```json
{
  "strategy": "percentage",
  "versions": [
    {"version_id": "demo-api-v2", "percentage": 10},
    {"version_id": "demo-api-v1", "percentage": 90}
  ]
}
```

This puts `demo-api-v2` live for 10% of traffic while `demo-api-v1` serves the remaining 90%. The percentages total 100, which the API requires. A couple of things worth knowing: the split is applied per request rather than per user, so a single visitor can hit both versions across requests; and if you later want to roll back, you can deploy `demo-api-v1` at 100% rather than deleting this deployment.

I created a percentage-strategy deployment for the Worker `demo-api` that sends 10% of traffic to `demo-api-v2` and 90% to `demo-api-v1`. The call was a dry run, so the deployment was not actually created.

